==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
Formed from the numeral {{term|tíu|lang=is}}, perhaps by directly reanalizing the ''-u'' as the weak feminine oblique suffix in environments where ''tíu'' is the object in a sentence. Compare {{term|nía|lang=is}} and {{term|átta|lang=is}}, also {{term|fimma|lang=is}}, {{term|sexa|lang=is}}, {{term|sjöa|lang=is}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtʰiːja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːja|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|tíu|tíur}}

# [[ten]] {{gloss|playing card, bus, etc., numbered 10}}

====Declension====
